{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The problem does not contain a sure outcome (i.e., no 100% probability outcome), so the reference value is zero. The reason evaluates the mean difference between each outcome and the reference value (i.e., the outcomes themselves, since reference = 0), weighted by their probabilities. For Lottery A: (4000 - 0)*0.25 + (2000 - 0)*0.25 + (0 - 0)*0.50 = 1000 + 500 + 0 = 1500. For Lottery B: (6000 - 0)*0.25 + (0 - 0)*0.75 = 1500 + 0 = 1500. The mean differences are equal (1500 for both), so the reason would be indifferent between A and B.",
